      "suggestion": "Change the measured compartment from recovered (R) peak to acutely infected (I) or quitters (Cq) peak (or to a final-size / R0-related summary), so that 'everyone adheres' actually shows whether spread stops; or retitle the level to 'Adherence increases recovery' to match the recovered-peak outcome.",
      "term": "dr/dt of R does not contain theta; the effect on R peak is emergent and does not show R0<1"
